2026-06-01 16:31:44.271 [TestNG-tests-1] INFO  core.controller.MobileUIController - y plan electrical fault finding mains power on this test consists of two checks 1 make sure there is no demand for heating inspect the indicator lever on the side of the diverter valve at rest with no demand the lever should be in the w position is the valve at w with a water only demand 2 if the system is cold place a demand for hot water and monitor the temperature of the radiators does the temperature of the radiators increase during a hot water only demand valve does not reach w position with demand for hot water only valve at w position but radiators heat with hot water demand jump to page send feedback go to home yplanvalve150 gif highlight circle 555054dualtimerhw200 gif cylstatmax100 gif system2 gif note if the system is already hot it may be difficult to gauge an increase in the pipe temperature you can cool the system quickly by partially draining and refilling with cool water you should also question the customer as to the symptoms of the fault
