2026-06-15 16:07:07.675 [TestNG-tests-1] INFO  core.controller.MobileUIController - common pump faults pump failure 2017 v2 this guide is intended to help identify the cause of pump failures and possible solutions to prevent reoccurrence common pump failures system water quality e g sludge 10 the pump is lubricated and cooled by the water flowing through it sludge in the water will get into the bearings and motor restricting the flow through the internal parts of the pump which will cause 10 the bearings to run dry and the pump 10 to become hot and the motor to 10 eventually seize 10 10 restrictions in circulation 10 if the flow circulation is restricted it can cause excessive pump load 10 e g trvs fitted s plan etc 10 ensure a properly adjusted by pass is fitted 10 10 open vented systems check that the cold feed and open vent are configured and positioned correctly 150mm apart max and that the header tank is filled to the correct level 10 10 sealed systems ensure that the cold system pressure is approximately 1 5bar angle of installation the preferred arrangement is where the pump is installed in a vertical pipe pumping upwards with the pump shaft horizontal a pump installed in horizontal pipe work should be fitted on its side so that the pump shaft is horizontal or slightly higher at the vent plug end this reduces the load on the bearings and ensures air can be purged from both the rotor chamber and impeller housing the pump should not be positioned with the body vertical as this can lead to the top bearing running dry which would cause noise and premature pump failure pumprotation pumprotationb bgpumprig1 20200 diaglabverticalwatermark
