2026-10-12 15:08:47.658 [TestNG-tests-1] INFO  core.controller.mobile.MobileUIController - common pump faults pump failure 2017 v2 this guide is intended to help identify the cause of pump failures and possible solutions to prevent reoccurrence common pump failures angle of installation the preferred arrangement is where the pump is installed in a vertical pipe pumping upwards with the pump shaft horizontal a pump installed in horizontal pipe work should be fitted on its side so that the pump shaft is horizontal or slightly higher at the vent plug end this reduces the load on the bearings and ensures air can be purged from both the rotor chamber and impeller housing the pump should not be positioned with the body vertical as this can lead to the top bearing running dry which would cause noise and premature pump failure pumprotation pumprotationb bgpumprig1 20200 diaglabverticalwatermark
